{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"openSUSE-SU-2026:22450-1","published":"2026-11-24T08:38:06Z","modified":"2026-11-27T17:23:18.082384634Z","related":["CVE-2026-113425","CVE-2026-118899","CVE-2026-120967","CVE-2026-121810","CVE-2026-123007","CVE-2026-123633","CVE-2026-123634","CVE-2026-123640","CVE-2026-125283"],"upstream":["CVE-2026-113425","CVE-2026-118899","CVE-2026-120967","CVE-2026-121810","CVE-2026-123007","CVE-2026-123633","CVE-2026-123634","CVE-2026-123640","CVE-2026-125283"],"summary":"Security update for nginx","details":"This update for nginx fixes the following issues:\n\n- CVE-2026-113425: use-after-free in mail proxy module (bsc#1290874).\n- CVE-2026-118899: infinite loop while reading client request body over TLS 1.3 (bsc#1290873).\n- CVE-2026-120967: SNI bypass when using client certificate validation in stream (bsc#1290877).\n- CVE-2026-121810: use-after-free in HTTP/3 (bsc#1290871).\n- CVE-2026-123007: memory corruption in HTTP/2 flow control (bsc#1290868).\n- CVE-2026-123633: use-after-free in HTTP/2 (bsc#1290872).\n- CVE-2026-123634: use-after-free during response processing in resolver (bsc#1290867).\n- CVE-2026-123640: insufficient validation in stream ssl_preread module (bsc#1290878).\n- CVE-2026-125283: buffer overflow when using alias with try_files (bsc#1290876).\n","affected":[{"package":{"name":"nginx","ecosystem":"openSUSE:Leap 16.1","purl":"pkg:rpm/opensuse/nginx&distro=openSUSE%20Leap%2016.1"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"1.27.2-160100.3.1"}]}],"ecosystem_specific":{"binaries":[{"nginx":"1.27.2-160100.3.1","nginx-source":"1.27.2-160100.3.1"}]},"database_specific":{"source":"https://ftp.suse.com/pub/projects/security/osv/openSUSE-SU-2026:22450-1.json"}}],"references":[{"type":"ADVISORY"},{"type":"REPORT","url":"https://bugzilla.suse.com/1290867"},{"type":"REPORT","url":"https://bugzilla.suse.com/1290868"},{"type":"REPORT","url":"https://bugzilla.suse.com/1290871"},{"type":"REPORT","url":"https://bugz